CM TM-WHP-NEC-008
CM 5.6m telescopic whip retracted, 6m band (50.000-54.000 MHz)
CM ---------------------------------------------------------------
CM Antenna: 7-section telescopic whip, retracted to 1.40m
CM   QW at 52.000 MHz = c/(4*f) * vf = 1.44m * 0.97 ~ 1.40m
CM   No loading coil; whip trimmed to QW resonance at ~52 MHz
CM
CM Wire geometry:
CM   GW 1: main whip, 20 segs, z=0.005 to z=1.405, radius=0.003m
CM          (radius reduced — fewer sections extended, thinner rod)
CM   GW 2: radial +X, z=0.005, length=1.40m, radius=0.003m
CM   GW 3: radial -X, z=0.005, length=1.40m, radius=0.003m
CM   GW 4: radial +Y, z=0.005, length=1.40m, radius=0.003m
CM   GW 5: radial -Y, z=0.005, length=1.40m, radius=0.003m
CM
CM Ground: real average soil (GN 2), sigma=0.005 S/m, epsilon_r=13
CM Feed: voltage source EX 0 on segment 1 of GW1 (base of whip)
CM No LD card — resonant retracted whip
CM
CM Note: At 6m the segment length / wavelength ratio is ~0.036
CM   NEC-2 accuracy acceptable; ratio well within lambda/10 guideline
CM   Reduced wire radius (0.003m) reflects thinner upper sections
CM   Expected Z ~ 35-50 ohms at resonance
CE
GW 1 20  0.0 0.0 0.005  0.0 0.0 1.405  0.003
GW 2 10  0.0 0.0 0.005  1.40 0.0 0.005  0.003
GW 3 10  0.0 0.0 0.005 -1.40 0.0 0.005  0.003
GW 4 10  0.0 0.0 0.005  0.0 1.40 0.005  0.003
GW 5 10  0.0 0.0 0.005  0.0 -1.40 0.005  0.003
GE 1
GN 2 0 0 0  13 0.005
EX 0 1 1 0  1 0
FR 0 9 0 0  50.000 0.500
RP 0 37 73 1000  0 0 5 5
EN
